course: dictionary
lesson: 2665
title: Dew: tiny drops of water
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dew is tiny drops of water that form on grass, leaves and other cool things outside. You see it most often at night or early in the morning. Context helps you spot it: «A spider web covered in dew is a trap for flies and also beautiful.» The web is wet with tiny drops, and it shines in the morning.
explain: Scientists have a name for how dew forms: condensation. At night the ground cools down. Water vapour in the air then turns into liquid drops on the cool grass. The water comes from the air, not from rain falling from the sky.
explain: Writers use dew to make mornings sound fresh and sparkling. Read the clue carefully: «A sundew's leaves have red hairs tipped with sticky drops that glitter like dew.» Glitter like dew means the drops shine like tiny wet lights.
fact: Dew is tiny drops of water that form on cool surfaces outside, such as grass and leaves.
fact: Dew usually forms at night or early in the morning.
fact: Dew is uncountable, so say «some dew» or «morning dew», not «a dew» or «dews».
fact: Dew forms by condensation: water vapour in the air turns into liquid drops when the ground cools.
fact: Useful phrases include «wet with dew», «dewdrop» and «dew point».
exercise: «Garden spiders build round webs that are big by autumn, dew makes the silk easy to see.» What is dew? | A kind of insect that spins silk | A type of cloud that floats high in the sky | *Tiny drops of water on cool surfaces, usually at night or early morning
exercise: Where does dew usually form? | In the middle of a hot desert afternoon | Inside the kitchen at lunchtime | *On grass and leaves outside, at night or early in the morning
exercise: «A sundew's leaves have red hairs tipped with sticky drops that glitter like dew.» Find and copy one word that means shine with little flashes of light. | *glitter | leaves | hairs | sticky
test: «It doesn't run backwards, because wet grass can also come from a sprinkler, dew or a dog.» Name one thing, other than dew, that can make grass wet. | A fish | A rainbow | *A sprinkler | A teacher
test: Why does dew form at night? | Because birds drop water on the leaves | Because the wind blows the rain away | Because the sun melts the grass | *Because the ground cools and water vapour in the air turns into liquid drops
exam: Which sentence uses dew correctly? | *There was dew on the grass this morning | The dews were on the grass this morning | There was a dew on the grass this morning
